          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On August 31, 2010, around 11:10 PM, a witness observed a flickering red light moving at a constant speed along a linear trajectory in the sky. The particularly long and gradual flickering intrigued the witness. With low strangeness and good consistency given the precision of the testimony, this observation case cannot be concluded without additional information. The hypothesis of an aircraft with particular lighting could fit, but could not be confirmed (see the investigation report). This case is classified C due to lack of independent testimonies and cross-checks.",
